**Convention 2.5 (finite COMPLETE).** The observer has one source-independent initialization and fixed time-homogeneous source-independent acquired-letter kernels. COMPLETE counts the original control and records, private labels, program, installed tables and their numerical representation, model selectors, workspace, addresses, output indices, sampler states and all persistent randomness. Runtime reads one actual finite configuration. There is no uncounted tape, posterior or probability-row port, clock, archive, advice, continuous hidden register, source-correlated seed or exact-real oracle. Synthetic generation makes no source call and uses the same acquired update after each generated letter. For any legal operation $o$ and residual event $E$, the full law satisfies $D_z(oE)=q_z(o)\sum_{z'}P_o(z,z')D_{z'}(E)$, including at $q_z(o)=0$. The cylinder includes the original operation block; a zero synthetic probability does not delete the actual update or a legal actual history. Rational representations are considered in Proposition 7.1.

